course: dictionary
lesson: 2520
title: Declarations: words that announce
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A declaration is a statement that says something clearly, so that everyone can hear or read it. When you meet the word, look at the words around it. «Independence Day in the USA remembers the Declaration of Independence of 1776.» The capital letters, the date and the word Independence tell you this is an important written document.
explain: The clues in the sentence show which kind of declaration it is. «The Universal Declaration of Human Rights was adopted in 1948.» That is a formal document. But when someone says «a declaration of love», it is a personal statement made out loud, not a document. Always ask: what was declared, and who was it for?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «The king made a declaration to his people.» If you swap in "a clear, official announcement", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: A declaration is an official or important statement that says something clearly to everyone.
fact: A declaration can be a written document, such as the «Declaration of Independence» of 1776 in the USA.
fact: A «declaration of love» is when someone tells another person that they love them.
fact: The «Universal Declaration of Human Rights» was adopted in 1948, and it names rights that belong to everyone.
fact: Phrases to know: make a declaration, declaration of war, declaration of independence.
exercise: «Independence Day in the USA remembers the Declaration of Independence of 1776.» What is a declaration here? | A song sung at a party | A kind of holiday food | A quiet whisper to a friend | *An official written document
exercise: Maya says, «He made a declaration of love to her.» What does this mean? | He wrote a form for the post office | He lost his way on the walk | He stopped talking for a while | *He told her clearly that he loved her
exercise: In which year was the «Universal Declaration of Human Rights» adopted? | 1776 | *1948 | 1066 | 2007
test: «Customs declaration» appears on forms at the airport. What is a declaration on a form? | A type of passport photo | A dance move | A map of the airport | *An official statement of what you are bringing
test: The UN adopted a «Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples» in which year? | 1776 | 1066 | 1948 | *2007
exam: In «a declaration of war», what does declaration mean? | *A clear, formal announcement that something is happening | A list of shopping | A gentle hug | A game played outdoors
